  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu Humanitarian Response Recovery and Preparedness Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HRRP would support local, GoV leadership in delivering a strategic, systematic, Vanuatu led approach to disaster preparedness, response, and recovery.  It would enable Vanuatu to be able to optimize the finance and programs opportunities at its disposal.  It would be a long-term program, embedding personnel within government, allowing relationships and trust, and understanding of the political economy, which are critical to success in Vanuatu, to be built. It would have an activity budget allowing it to fund activities and technical advisory support.  It would have the capacity to expand its resources in response to disasters and support post to effectively deliver Humanitarian Emergency Funds (HEF) and other sources of funds that become available when disaster occur.  It would be flexible, well attuned to changes in the political economy, and able to invest in opportunities as they arise, and walk away from ones that meet resistance.</narrative>
  </description>
